@startuml FRQ-AUD-01-audit-record-path
' Viewpoint: audit record path, component -> sink. Audience: developer, architect.
' A view, not a source of truth (D-13). Labels: UK English.
' Scope: the SPECIFIED path. Steps 2-6 are not implemented as of 2026-08-28 --
' the assembler flattens fields into the message before the handler is reached.
' What is in code per step: FRQ-AUD-01-audit-record-path.md SS5-SS6.
title FR-AUD-01 — Audit record path

start
:Component emits record\n(named AU-3 fields);
if (**kwargs splat?) then (yes)
  :Reject — input surface\nis not record surface;
  stop
else (no)
endif
:Assemble record;
:Classify each field\n(public / identity / measure / classified);
if (any handler subscribed?) then (no)
  :Warn once on default output;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
fork
  :Handler A — compare field class\nagainst declared capability;
  :Redact what capability\ndoes not cover;
  :Format and write to sink;
fork again
  :Handler B — same resolution,\ndifferent destination trust;
  :Format and write to sink;
end fork
if (write failed?) then (yes)
  :Raise handler failure event\n(to monitoring, not to caller);
  stop
else (no)
endif
:Record persisted per handler;
note right
  Records produced inside a handler
  never re-enter this path
  (recursion breaker).
end note
stop
@enduml
